From: Felipe Bonetto <felipesensbonetto@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xvc_server: add MODE_XPCU cable dispatch

openFPGALoader's --xvc server can drive a JTAG cable as a TCP-exposed
XVC endpoint, but the cable-mode dispatch in src/xvc_server.cpp's
ctor only enables MODE_FTDI_SERIAL and MODE_LIBGPIOD_BITBANG. The
Xilinx Platform Cable USB II driver (MODE_XPCU) exists for the
program flow but isn't wired into the XVC server, so
  `openFPGALoader --xvc --cable xilinxPlatformCableUsb ...`
fails with "Jtag: unknown cable type".

This patch:
  - includes xilinxPlatformCableUSB.hpp,
  - drops the (void)firmware_path; discard since we now use it,
  - adds a case MODE_XPCU instantiating XilinxPlatformCableUSB exactly
    as src/jtag.cpp does for the program path.

--- a/src/xvc_server.cpp
+++ b/src/xvc_server.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,9 @@
 #include "ftdiJtagMPSSE.hpp"
 #ifdef ENABLE_LIBGPIOD
 #include "libgpiodJtagBitbang.hpp"
+#endif
+#ifdef ENABLE_XILINX_PLATFORM_CABLE_USB
+#include "xilinxPlatformCableUSB.hpp"
 #endif
 #include "cable.hpp"
 #include "display.hpp"
@@ -30,7 +33,6 @@
 {
 	(void)pin_conf;
 	(void)ip_adr;
-	(void)firmware_path;
 	switch (cable.type) {
 	case MODE_FTDI_SERIAL:
 		_jtag = new FtdiJtagMPSSE(cable, dev, serial, clkHZ,
@@ -76,6 +78,15 @@
 		break;
 #endif
 #endif
+	case MODE_XPCU:
+#ifdef ENABLE_XILINX_PLATFORM_CABLE_USB
+		_jtag = new XilinxPlatformCableUSB(0x03fd, 0x0013, clkHZ,
+			firmware_path, _verbose);
+		break;
+#else
+		std::cerr << "XVC server: support for Xilinx Platform Cable USB (XPCU) was not enabled at compile time" << std::endl;
+		throw std::exception();
+#endif
 	default:
 		std::cerr << "Jtag: unknown cable type" << std::endl;
 		throw std::exception();
